From 161d7b6752cba2f115f1bb4b3f4246b7f7a3764e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:17:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cron,gateway): cron honours the core-update admission
 fence; a drain restart is cancelled when its update gives up [daveey]

A cron job due inside a hermes-sync drain window started under the admission hold (cron took only the
process retirement fence), held the gateway's deferred restart open past the window, and when the
updater gave up the restart still ran on the old code (David-MBP 2026-10-29 15:29-15:47, t_01a189db034f3b2b).

- cron tick takes the cross-process admission reservation for its scan/advance/submit; while the hold
  stands it dispatches nothing and due jobs stay due (nothing advanced).
- each cron run holds its own reservation (admission_fence.extend, taken inside the tick's) for its
  whole life, so the drainer's reservation read sees it and never publishes the intent under it.
- gateway: a restart requested while <home>/core-update/intent exists is cancelled if the intent goes
  away before the work drains (the update gave up), instead of relaunching the old code.
